I hear the double bluff. You hold a little back to see who’ll notice there’s more. Then when people take you at face value, it can feel like they saw all you had to offer and passed. They may have just believed the version you gave them.

And I think I played into it a little. You asked what role you play, and I went straight to what you do for people. You get things moving. You make the call. But “I’m ready to shine” sounded more like I want you to see what I can do when I stop holding back. That’s a different thing to say out loud, especially to people who already think they know you.